{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Live DC harness (rendered HTML) + cross-repo contract test\n\n## Context / Problem\nThe DC codec is validated offline against pandoc's jira reader as a proxy, but the\nreal Jira DC wiki renderer and Jira's own storage canonicalization differ from pandoc\nand cannot be modeled offline — that gap is the residual risk this story closes. The\nrepo already runs live DC testing with a Dockerized Jira 8.17.1 instance in GitHub\nActions (`tests/external/live_jira_dc/`), so this extends that harness rather than\nbuilding a new one. Separately, the sibling repo `agentic-dev-platform` imports the\n`InboundMapper.normalize_rich_text` seam from this package, so changing its behavior\nmust be guarded by a contract test.\n\nThis story is the LIVE proof of the state-based echo-safety and settled-conflict\nbehavior that `5c0e` (DC render robustness) and `3388` (cutover + echo suppression +\nlocal-wins conflict) deliver; it depends on both.\n\n## Approach\nExtend the existing Docker DC harness with a rich-text test that:\n- renders a representative body and pushes it via the real API\n  (`rebar.edit_ticket(local_id, repo_root=repo, description=value)`, the pattern\n  already used by `_out_description` in\n  `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py`), and asserts **rendered HTML**\n  through `?expand=renderedFields` — not just the wiki source via `?fields=description`\n  — so we verify what Jira actually interprets (`*foo*`→bold, `h1.`→heading,\n  `{code}`→macro). No `renderedFields`/`expand=` assertion exists in the harness\n  today, so this is a genuinely new fidelity check.\n- runs a second reconcile pass to assert **state-based echo-safety end-to-end** (the\n  landed rich body decodes to a value the differ recognizes as unchanged → no\n  re-push), exercising `3388`'s once-only-upgrade-then-converge path against the real\n  renderer.\n- performs a **Jira-side edit** to assert `3388`'s settled concurrency behavior: the\n  next pass keeps rebar's body (**local-wins**) AND surfaces the divergence as the\n  existing deduped `outbound-field-conflict` bridge alert — the remote value is\n  recorded, never silently destroyed (NOT a novel LWW clock; this is the a713 +\n  `3388` policy proven live).\n\nGate it with the harness's existing skip markers (absent-harness / absent-extra) and\nthe session-scoped PAT the harness already provisions. Add a contract test that pins\nthe public shape/behavior of `normalize_rich_text`\n(`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py:134`, exposed as\n`InboundMapper.normalize_rich_text`) so a change that would break the\n`agentic-dev-platform` import fails here first.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/` — new rich-text live test module (render+push,\n  `?expand=renderedFields` HTML assertions, 2nd-pass echo, Jira-side-edit local-wins\n  + conflict-alert assertion), reusing the existing conftest fixtures/skip markers.\n- CI workflow for the DC harness job — ensure the new test runs in the existing\n  amd64 Docker job (no new job).\n- `tests/` — cross-repo `normalize_rich_text` contract test.\n\n## Testing\n- Live render fidelity: a pushed rich body's `renderedFields` HTML contains the\n  expected bold/heading/code-macro markup (skipped when the harness/extra is absent).\n- Live echo-safety: a second reconcile pass against the live instance pushes no\n  description change (upgrade-then-converge holds against the real renderer).\n- Live conflict: a Jira-side edit between passes keeps rebar's body and raises the\n  `outbound-field-conflict` bridge alert (remote value recorded, not clobbered).\n- Contract: `normalize_rich_text` accepts the documented inputs and returns the\n  documented type/shape; a signature/behavior change fails\n  `test_normalize_rich_text_contract`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The Docker DC harness has a rich-text test asserting rendered HTML via\n  `?expand=renderedFields` (not just wiki source), covering bold/heading/code-macro;\n  verified by the test running in the existing DC-harness CI job.\n- [ ] The live test asserts state-based echo-safety across a second pass (no re-push)\n  AND `3388`'s settled local-wins + `outbound-field-conflict` bridge alert on a\n  Jira-side edit (remote value recorded, not silently destroyed); verified by the\n  same live test.\n- [ ] A cross-repo contract test pins `normalize_rich_text`\n  (`InboundMapper.normalize_rich_text`) back-compat so a breaking change fails here\n  first; verified by `test_normalize_rich_text_contract`."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785821562158394001,"uuid":"0c4b7b0a-2980-4e72-b0d6-5543489f4bbd"}